{"additional":"","additionalPlain":"","categories":{"commitment":"Permanent contract & B2B","department":"Consulting","location":"Warsaw","team":"Polska Team","allLocations":["Warsaw"]},"createdAt":1787056897672,"descriptionPlain":"Project Manager / PMO – ERP Transformation Program (Oracle Fusion Cloud)\nReporting directly to the IT Program Director, this role serves as operational support for leadership. The individual will be responsible for maintaining a cohesive, cross-functional overview of the ERP/EPM transformation program (SAP ECC / BFC / Anaplan to Oracle Fusion Cloud), including work progress, capacity, key metrics, and defects. The role involves aggregating, verifying, and translating data provided by Scrum Masters and Stream Leads into decision-making materials for governance bodies.\nScope of Duties:\nOngoing progress tracking: Consolidating statuses across various streams (milestones, deliverables, dependencies), maintaining the program schedule and resource workload plan, and flagging variances.\nCapacity planning: Building and maintaining the capacity plan: forecasted workload per stream, availability of IT teams, business units, and the integrator, as well as anticipating peak operational periods (testing, cutover). Monitoring actual utilization against the plan.\nKPIs and reporting: Defining and evolving executive metrics, preparing dashboards, and creating materials for status committees and governance boards.\nDefect management: Maintaining a consolidated view of defects in JIRA: triage, prioritization, assignment to streams, and monitoring metrics (volume, severity, age of tickets) along with phase exit criteria.\nRisks and alerts: Maintaining the program risk register, formalizing action plans, and monitoring their execution.\nRequirements:\nProven experience in the operational delivery of IT programs or in a PMO role, preferably within the ERP domain (Oracle Fusion Cloud is a strong plus).\nStrong understanding of ERP testing cycles (SIT, UAT, cutover testing) and experience in coordinating testing campaigns across multi-team environments: consolidating progress, monitoring execution and efficacy metrics, and tracking phase exit criteria.\nHands-on experience in building and managing capacity/workload plans.\nProven ability to define KPIs, build reports, and prepare presentation decks for governance meetings.\nAdvanced proficiency in JIRA and Microsoft Excel; working knowledge of Power BI is highly desirable.\nStrong risk management capabilities, excellent analytical and synthesis skills, and high autonomy.\n","description":"<div>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"9\">Project Manager / PMO – ERP Transformation Program (Oracle Fusion Cloud)</h2>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"10\">Reporting directly to the IT Program Director, this role serves as operational support for leadership. The individual will be responsible for maintaining a cohesive, cross-functional overview of the ERP/EPM transformation program (SAP ECC / BFC / Anaplan to Oracle Fusion Cloud), including work progress, capacity, key metrics, and defects. The role involves aggregating, verifying, and translating data provided by Scrum Masters and Stream Leads into decision-making materials for governance bodies.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"11\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"11\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Scope of Duties:</strong></p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"12\">\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"12,0,0\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"12,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Ongoing progress tracking:</strong> Consolidating statuses across various streams (milestones, deliverables, dependencies), maintaining the program schedule and resource workload plan, and flagging variances.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"12,1,0\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"12,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Capacity planning:</strong> Building and maintaining the capacity plan: forecasted workload per stream, availability of IT teams, business units, and the integrator, as well as anticipating peak operational periods (testing, cutover). Monitoring actual utilization against the plan.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"12,2,0\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"12,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">KPIs and reporting:</strong> Defining and evolving executive metrics, preparing dashboards, and creating materials for status committees and governance boards.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"12,3,0\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"12,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Defect management:</strong> Maintaining a consolidated view of defects in JIRA: triage, prioritization, assignment to streams, and monitoring metrics (volume, severity, age of tickets) along with phase exit criteria.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"12,4,0\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"12,4,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Risks and alerts:</strong> Maintaining the program risk register, formalizing action plans, and monitoring their execution.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"13\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"13\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"14\">\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14,0,0\">Proven experience in the operational delivery of IT programs or in a PMO role, preferably within the ERP domain (Oracle Fusion Cloud is a strong plus).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14,1,0\">Strong understanding of ERP testing cycles (SIT, UAT, cutover testing) and experience in coordinating testing campaigns across multi-team environments: consolidating progress, monitoring execution and efficacy metrics, and tracking phase exit criteria.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14,2,0\">Hands-on experience in building and managing capacity/workload plans.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14,3,0\">Proven ability to define KPIs, build reports, and prepare presentation decks for governance meetings.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14,4,0\">Advanced proficiency in JIRA and Microsoft Excel; working knowledge of Power BI is highly desirable.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14,5,0\">Strong risk management capabilities, excellent analytical and synthesis skills, and high autonomy.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>","id":"3ca57973-f0f0-499b-9ba0-b4cbb8d4bbf1","lists":[],"salaryRange":{"min":155,"max":185,"interval":"per-hour-wage","currency":"PLN"},"text":"Project Manager / PMO – ERP Transformation Program (Oracle Fusion Cloud)","country":"PL","workplaceType":"remote","opening":"","openingPlain":"","descriptionBody":"<div>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"9\">Project Manager / PMO &ndash; ERP Transformation Program (Oracle Fusion Cloud)</h2>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"10\">Reporting directly to the IT Program Director, this role serves as operational support for leadership. The individual will be responsible for maintaining a cohesive, cross-functional overview of the ERP/EPM transformation program (SAP ECC / BFC / Anaplan to Oracle Fusion Cloud), including work progress, capacity, key metrics, and defects. The role involves aggregating, verifying, and translating data provided by Scrum Masters and Stream Leads into decision-making materials for governance bodies.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"11\"><strong data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"11\">Scope of Duties:</strong></p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"12\">\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"12,0,0\"><strong data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"12,0,0\">Ongoing progress tracking:</strong> Consolidating statuses across various streams (milestones, deliverables, dependencies), maintaining the program schedule and resource workload plan, and flagging variances.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"12,1,0\"><strong data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"12,1,0\">Capacity planning:</strong> Building and maintaining the capacity plan: forecasted workload per stream, availability of IT teams, business units, and the integrator, as well as anticipating peak operational periods (testing, cutover). Monitoring actual utilization against the plan.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"12,2,0\"><strong data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"12,2,0\">KPIs and reporting:</strong> Defining and evolving executive metrics, preparing dashboards, and creating materials for status committees and governance boards.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"12,3,0\"><strong data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"12,3,0\">Defect management:</strong> Maintaining a consolidated view of defects in JIRA: triage, prioritization, assignment to streams, and monitoring metrics (volume, severity, age of tickets) along with phase exit criteria.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"12,4,0\"><strong data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"12,4,0\">Risks and alerts:</strong> Maintaining the program risk register, formalizing action plans, and monitoring their execution.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"13\"><strong data-index-in-node=\"0\" data-path-to-node=\"13\">Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"14\">\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14,0,0\">Proven experience in the operational delivery of IT programs or in a PMO role, preferably within the ERP domain (Oracle Fusion Cloud is a strong plus).</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14,1,0\">Strong understanding of ERP testing cycles (SIT, UAT, cutover testing) and experience in coordinating testing campaigns across multi-team environments: consolidating progress, monitoring execution and efficacy metrics, and tracking phase exit criteria.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14,2,0\">Hands-on experience in building and managing capacity/workload plans.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14,3,0\">Proven ability to define KPIs, build reports, and prepare presentation decks for governance meetings.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14,4,0\">Advanced proficiency in JIRA and Microsoft Excel; working knowledge of Power BI is highly desirable.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14,5,0\">Strong risk management capabilities, excellent analytical and synthesis skills, and high autonomy.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"Project Manager / PMO – ERP Transformation Program (Oracle Fusion Cloud)\nReporting directly to the IT Program Director, this role serves as operational support for leadership. The individual will be responsible for maintaining a cohesive, cross-functional overview of the ERP/EPM transformation program (SAP ECC / BFC / Anaplan to Oracle Fusion Cloud), including work progress, capacity, key metrics, and defects. The role involves aggregating, verifying, and translating data provided by Scrum Masters and Stream Leads into decision-making materials for governance bodies.\nScope of Duties:\nOngoing progress tracking: Consolidating statuses across various streams (milestones, deliverables, dependencies), maintaining the program schedule and resource workload plan, and flagging variances.\nCapacity planning: Building and maintaining the capacity plan: forecasted workload per stream, availability of IT teams, business units, and the integrator, as well as anticipating peak operational periods (testing, cutover). Monitoring actual utilization against the plan.\nKPIs and reporting: Defining and evolving executive metrics, preparing dashboards, and creating materials for status committees and governance boards.\nDefect management: Maintaining a consolidated view of defects in JIRA: triage, prioritization, assignment to streams, and monitoring metrics (volume, severity, age of tickets) along with phase exit criteria.\nRisks and alerts: Maintaining the program risk register, formalizing action plans, and monitoring their execution.\nRequirements:\nProven experience in the operational delivery of IT programs or in a PMO role, preferably within the ERP domain (Oracle Fusion Cloud is a strong plus).\nStrong understanding of ERP testing cycles (SIT, UAT, cutover testing) and experience in coordinating testing campaigns across multi-team environments: consolidating progress, monitoring execution and efficacy metrics, and tracking phase exit criteria.\nHands-on experience in building and managing capacity/workload plans.\nProven ability to define KPIs, build reports, and prepare presentation decks for governance meetings.\nAdvanced proficiency in JIRA and Microsoft Excel; working knowledge of Power BI is highly desirable.\nStrong risk management capabilities, excellent analytical and synthesis skills, and high autonomy.\n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/margo-group/3ca57973-f0f0-499b-9ba0-b4cbb8d4bbf1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/margo-group/3ca57973-f0f0-499b-9ba0-b4cbb8d4bbf1/apply"}